# Value Added Tax Proclamation No. 1341/2024 — የተጨማሪ እሴት ታክስ አዋጅ ቁጥር 1341/2016

Federal Negarit Gazette 30th Year No. 61, Addis Ababa, 21 August 2024; in force on its approval by the House of Peoples' Representatives (Art. 75). Repeals the Value Added Tax Proclamation No. 285/2002 (Art. 73(3)), which still applies to accounting periods before this law began (Art. 74). From the Ministry of Revenue's bilingual PDF on mor.gov.et; the English column is reproduced below and the Amharic column is a separate file in this library. The Ministry's PDF ends at the signature: Schedules 1–3 (zero-rated supplies, exempt supplies, exempt imports) are not in it, so the lists of exempt and zero-rated items are not reproduced here.

## What this law covers (in brief)

Who must charge VAT and at what rate, compulsory and voluntary registration, suspension and cancellation of registration, when and where a supply happens, the value of supplies and imports, input tax credits and refunds, tax invoices, monthly VAT returns and payment, VAT withholding by government bodies, and VAT penalties.

## Key articles

- Art. 8 — VAT is charged on taxable supplies by registered persons, taxable imports, and reverse-charged supplies (services from abroad) received by a registered person, government entity or large unregistered person. The rate is 15%, or 0% for a zero-rated supply.
- Art. 9–11 — zero-rated supplies (Schedule 1), exempt supplies (Schedule 2) and exempt imports (Schedule 3).
- Art. 12 — compulsory registration when taxable supplies in any 12 months exceed, or are expected to exceed, the registration threshold of Birr 2,000,000 (or another amount set by a Ministry directive). Sales of capital goods and a one-off sale or closure of the business are not counted. Apply in the approved form within 7 days of becoming liable. Government entities are not required to register but may register voluntarily.
- Art. 13 — voluntary registration is possible only if annual taxable supplies exceed Birr 1,000,000 (or an amount set by directive).
- Art. 15 — the original VAT certificate is displayed at the main premises and an official copy at every other premises; VAT details must appear on websites and social media accounts used for the business.
- Art. 16 — a registered person who stops making taxable supplies notifies the authority within 7 days; the authority cancels, or suspends for up to 12 months if the business will restart.
- Art. 17 — a registered person below the threshold may apply for cancellation, but only 2 years after registration (earlier only if registered by mistake, before the first return is due).
- Art. 18 — on cancellation: stop presenting oneself as registered, file a final VAT return and pay within one month, and return the VAT certificate.
- Art. 52 — a registered person issues the original tax invoice at the time of a taxable supply; small cash sales and retailers may use a simplified invoice under limits set in the regulations.
- Art. 58–59 — a VAT return for every monthly accounting period, filed and paid by the last day of the following month, even when no VAT is payable. (Nehase and Pagume count as one month, Art. 2(1).)
- Art. 62 — a government entity buying from a registered person withholds 50% of the VAT, pays it to the tax authority and pays the other 50% to the supplier, who gets a credit for the withheld VAT.
- Art. 66 — penalties of Birr 100,000 for each failure such as not displaying the VAT certificate, not showing VAT details online, not notifying changes or cessation, or not issuing a credit or debit note; Birr 50,000 for each tax invoice or credit or debit note issued other than as the law provides. Other VAT penalties are in the Tax Administration Proclamation.
- Art. 74 — transitional: regulations and directives made under 285/2002 continue where consistent; a tour operator pays VAT for three years on the net fee for inbound tourism after costs in Ethiopia.

## በአማርኛ በአጭሩ — ይህ ሕግ ምን ይሸፍናል

የተጨማሪ እሴት ታክስ አዋጅ ቁጥር 1341/2016 (ነሐሴ 15 ቀን 2016 ዓ.ም.) የቀድሞውን አዋጅ ቁጥር 285/1994 ሽሯል። ማን ቫት መሰብሰብ እንዳለበት፣ ምጣኔው፣ ምዝገባና ስረዛ፣ የግብዓት ታክስ ማካካሻ፣ የታክስ ደረሰኝ፣ ወርሃዊ ማሳወቂያና ክፍያ፣ በመንግሥት መሥሪያ ቤቶች የሚቀነስ ቫትና ቅጣቶችን ይደነግጋል። የአማርኛው ሙሉ ጽሑፍ በዚህ ቤተ-መጻሕፍት በሌላ ፋይል አለ። ይህ ማጠቃለያ የሕጉ ኦፊሴላዊ ትርጉም አይደለም።

## ዋና ዋና ድንጋጌዎች

- አንቀጽ 8 — የተጨማሪ እሴት ታክስ ምጣኔ 15% ነው፤ ዜሮ ምጣኔ ለሚመለከታቸው አቅርቦቶች 0%።
- አንቀጽ 12 — በማናቸውም 12 ወራት ታክስ የሚከፈልበት አቅርቦት ከ2,000,000 ብር ከበለጠ ወይም እንደሚበልጥ ከታመነ መመዝገብ ግዴታ ነው፤ ግዴታው ከተጀመረ በ7 ቀናት ውስጥ ማመልከት አለበት።
- አንቀጽ 13 — በፈቃደኝነት መመዝገብ የሚቻለው ዓመታዊ አቅርቦቱ ከ1,000,000 ብር ሲበልጥ ነው።
- አንቀጽ 15 — ዋናው የቫት ምዝገባ ምስክር ወረቀት በዋናው የንግድ ቦታ፣ ቅጂው በሌሎች ቦታዎች ይለጠፋል፤ የቫት መረጃ በድረ-ገጽና በማህበራዊ ሚዲያ ላይ መገለጽ አለበት።
- አንቀጽ 16–18 — ታክስ የሚከፈልበትን አቅርቦት ያቆመ ሰው በ7 ቀናት ውስጥ ያሳውቃል፤ ከገደቡ በታች ሆኖ ስረዛ መጠየቅ የሚቻለው ከተመዘገበ 2 ዓመት በኋላ ነው፤ ምዝገባው ሲሰረዝ በአንድ ወር ውስጥ የመጨረሻ ማሳወቂያ አቅርቦ ይከፍላል፣ የምስክር ወረቀቱን ይመልሳል።
- አንቀጽ 52 — የተመዘገበ ሰው አቅርቦቱ በሚፈጸምበት ጊዜ የታክስ ደረሰኝ ይሰጣል።
- አንቀጽ 58–59 — ለእያንዳንዱ ወር ማሳወቂያ ቀርቦ ታክሱ በቀጣዩ ወር የመጨረሻ ቀን ይከፈላል፤ የሚከፈል ታክስ ባይኖርም ማሳወቂያ ግዴታ ነው።
- አንቀጽ 62 — የመንግሥት መሥሪያ ቤት ከተመዘገበ ሰው ሲገዛ የቫቱን 50% ቀንሶ ለታክስ ባለሥልጣኑ ይከፍላል።
- አንቀጽ 66 — የቫት ምስክር ወረቀት ያለመለጠፍ፣ ለውጥ ወይም ማቆምን ያለማሳወቅ ወዘተ ለእያንዳንዱ 100,000 ብር፤ ከሕጉ ውጪ ደረሰኝ መስጠት 50,000 ብር።
